Ladybird now takes the min-content and max-content widths of a replaced
box with a definite height from that height through its aspect ratio,
whatever the box’s own width. Run in Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox
151.0, and Playwright’s WebKit 26.5, all three engines keep an image
with width and height of 60px, whose natural size is 1x1, at 60x60 in a
flex container that has to shrink it.

Blink’s ComputeReplacedSizeInternal() derives the replaced inline
size from the definite height through InlineSizeFromAspectRatio()
for the content size suggestion. WebKit’s RenderReplaced::
computeAspectRatioAdjustedIntrinsicLogicalWidths() multiplies the
height by the ratio whenever hasReplacedLogicalHeight() holds. Gecko’s
nsLayoutUtils::IntrinsicForAxis() replaces the intrinsic size with the
ratio-dependent size of the definite height.
